---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageIntro from "../components/PageIntro.astro";
import { PROJECT_LINKS, repoFile } from "../config";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Lineage"
  description="The conceptual, repository, and licensing lineage from Softpowers to Servotab."
>
  <PageIntro
    index="03 / Lineage"
    title="Softpowers found the exponent. Servotab found how it applies force."
    description="Servotab keeps the strongest construction insight from Softpowers while giving the public product its own mechanism, name, domain, and visual world."
  />

  <section class="content-band" aria-labelledby="lineage-statement">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2 id="lineage-statement" class="lineage-statement">
        The task stays the base. <span>Method remains raised and conditional.</span>
      </h2>

      <div class="lineage-grid">
        <article>
          <span class="rail-label">inherit / Softpowers</span>
          <h2>Raised method</h2>
          <p>
            Softpowers established the task as the base and method as a smaller,
            raised operator. Servotab preserves that hierarchy, day-first clarity,
            evidence-scoped claims, and proportionate depth.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span class="rail-label">thesis / durable</span>
          <h2>Exponent, not machinery</h2>
          <p>
            Method modifies the work without replacing it. The user’s task,
            repository, permissions, and requested outcome remain authoritative.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span class="rail-label">transform / Servotab</span>
          <h2>Controlled leverage</h2>
          <p>
            The raised <span class="mono">p</span> becomes a raised <span class="mono">t</span>:
            both notation and a real tab—attached, directional, bounded, and able
            to change a larger trajectory before settling.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-band" aria-labelledby="independent-lineage-heading">
    <div class="shell content-layout">
      <p class="section-index">Independent lineage</p>
      <div class="content-prose">
        <h2 id="independent-lineage-heading">Shared problem domains. Independently written methods.</h2>
        <p>
          The project began as an independent rewrite inspired by{" "}
          <a href="https://github.com/obra/superpowers">obra/superpowers</a>.
          It works across familiar engineering domains while independently defining
          its activation model, progressive disclosure, workflow thresholds, testing
          policy, review shape, delegation contract, and verification scope.
        </p>
        <p>
          Additional method references and retained terminology are recorded in{" "}
          the repository’s <a href={repoFile("THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md")}>Third-Party Notices</a>.
          The <a href={repoFile("LICENSE-HISTORY.md")}>License History</a> preserves
          the forward-only licensing boundary across earlier revisions.
        </p>
        <p><a href={PROJECT_LINKS.source}>Inspect the current source and preserved history</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-band content-band-ink" aria-labelledby="retired-heading">
    <div class="shell content-layout">
      <p class="section-index">Retired identity</p>
      <div class="content-prose">
        <h2 id="retired-heading">The lineage stays visible. The product moves forward.</h2>
        <p>
          Servotab is not presented as a lighter “power-up,” a cockpit, or a fixed
          workflow system. The exponent survives because it still explains the
          relationship between task and method; the new tab explains how that
          small method acts with bounded force.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
